@startuml UC-34 Set Class Status - Sequence Diagram (icon)
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280
title 2.12.2.4 UC-34 Set Class Status — Sequence Diagram

actor Teacher
boundary ":ClassSettingsPage" as UI
control ":ClassController" as CTL
control ":ClassManagementService" as SVC
boundary ":ClassRepository" as REPO
database DB

autonumber
Teacher ->> UI : Open "Class settings" of an owned class and select "Archive class" or "Reactivate class"
activate UI
UI ->> UI : requestToggle()
UI -->> Teacher : Show the confirmation dialog with the target status and its effect

opt teacher cancels the change
  Teacher ->> UI : Close the confirmation dialog
  UI -->> Teacher : Keep the current class status and end the use case
end

Teacher ->> UI : Confirm the target status
UI ->> UI : confirmToggle()
UI ->> CTL : PATCH /api/classes/{id}/status
activate CTL
CTL ->> SVC : updateStatus(id, status)
activate SVC
SVC ->> REPO : findById(id)
activate REPO
REPO ->> DB : SELECT * FROM classes WHERE id = ?
activate DB
DB -->> REPO : row / none
deactivate DB
REPO -->> SVC : Classroom
deactivate REPO
SVC ->> SVC : accept only an existing class owned by the teacher whose status really changes, and require an assigned grade when reactivating

alt class is unavailable, not owned by the teacher or already in the target status
  SVC -->> CTL : ResourceNotFoundException / ForbiddenOperationException / IllegalArgumentException
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 404 / 403 / 400
  UI -->> Teacher : Show that the action is unavailable and keep the current status
else the target status differs and the teacher owns the class
  SVC ->> REPO : save(Classroom with the target status)
  activate REPO
  REPO ->> DB : UPDATE classes SET status = ?, updated_at = ? WHERE id = ?
  activate DB
  DB -->> REPO : Saved
  deactivate DB
  REPO -->> SVC : Classroom
  deactivate REPO
  SVC -->> CTL : ClassDetail
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 200 + ClassDetail
  UI -->> Teacher : Show MSG08 and the updated status, INACTIVE turning the class read-only
end
deactivate SVC
deactivate CTL
deactivate UI
@enduml
